{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>You overthrow those who rise against You.</b> He used the language of הריסה (overthrow/ruin) corresponding to how they (the Egyptians) forced them (Israel) in the building of bricks, and Scripture tells you measure for measure, for HaShem, blessed be He, overthrows them and does not build them, and this is the principle of כי בדבר אשר זדו עליהם. And it says קמיך (those who rise against You) when it should have said קמינו (against us) — but this comes to teach you that all who rise against Israel are as if they rise against the Shekhinah. And so David, peace be upon him, declared (Psalms 83:3): ״כי הנה אויביך יהמיון ומשנאיך נשאו ראש״, and he explained: why does he call them 'Your enemies' (אויביך) and 'those who hate You' (משנאיך)? Because ״על עמך יערימו סוד ויתיעצו על צפוניך״ — against Your people they craft a secret plot and take counsel against Your hidden ones."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:59:26.319064149Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}